{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Transformations.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Transformations.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender python transformations blender python transformations","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Transformations.md","fileName":"Blender Python Transformations.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Python Transformations","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Python Data and Operations]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Python Data and Operations","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Transformations.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Transformations.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender python transformations blender python transformations","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Transformations.md","fileName":"Blender Python Transformations.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Python Transformations","heading":"Blender Python Transformations","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Blender Python supports both imperative and declarative transformations. An operator can translate, rotate, or scale the selected objects by a differential amount, while assigning a location, rotation, or scale property directly sets the chosen object's state.\n\nThe distinction matters in loops and reusable toolkits. Repeated relative operators accumulate change and inherit the current selection and coordinate context; direct assignments overwrite known properties and can target a named datablock. Wrapping creation, deletion, and transformation in small utility functions can keep the main modeling algorithm focused on its data rather than repeated `bpy` setup.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Python Data and Operations","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Transformations.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Transformations.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender python transformations blender python transformations","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Transformations.md","fileName":"Blender Python Transformations.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Python Transformations","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[blenderpythonapi.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Python Data and Operations","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}